// chr(i) out of [0, 255] is a RUNTIME error (DEC-020): never a masked low
// byte. `chr(256)` and `chr(-1)` are rejected word-for-word the same on the
// four routes, the same no-silent-clipping contract as substr bounds
// (DEC-018) and s[i] (DEC-013).
// EXPECT-RUNTIME-ERROR: chr value 256 out of bounds (0..255)
fn main() {
    print(chr(256))
}
